ntradiction, but it's new factual info. The instruction says \"add facts not already adequately represented in C.\" A correction is new. It's directly supported by W5. It materially advances OneGap because it helps verify title/trophy status. So include.\n\nBut wait: The OneGap specifically: \"verify whether the 2023 article's fifteen-trophy claim matches Rangers rather than only the confirmed 13-signing/7-title facts.\" The W5 table gives 8 league titles, not 15. It might not \"match\" the fifteen-trophy claim, but it advances by showing league title count is 8, so 15 total trophies would include 7 other trophies. Is that a finding? The finding is simply 8 league championships. It doesn't verify fifteen. But it's a fact.\n\nShould we mention the table includes years? Yes.\n\nNeed output exactly JSON object matching schema. No extra text.\n\nLet's craft:\n{\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Rangers International (Enugu) has won 8 Nigeria Premier Football League championships, namely in 1974, 1975, 1977, 1981, 1982, 1984, 2016, and 2023–24.\",\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\"W5\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nCheck if \"Nigeria Premier Football League\" is the right league name? Source title \"Nigeria Premier Football League - Wikipedia\". Table says Championship. So okay.\n\nPotential second finding: \"Rangers International F.C. won the 2016 NPFL title as its 7th championship and the 2023–24 title as its 8th championship.\" But that's subsumed.\n\nCould include \"Enyimba has won 9 championships\" but not relevant to OneGap about Rangers. Avoid.\n\nMaybe include \"Rangers International (Enugu) is listed as having won 8 championships, ranking second behind Enyimba (9) in the most titles won table.\" That adds ranking. But OneGap doesn't need ranking. Not material.\n\nThus one finding.\n\nNeed ensure JSON valid. Use en dash in 2023–24. Fine.\n\nLet's final."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":883,"completion_tokens":1895,"total_tokens"